Immigration policies
3. The immigration policies of the Maldives shall be determined by the Minister.

Role of the Minister
4. (a) The most senior person who bears, on behalf of the Government, responsibility for all matters of providing immigration services in accordance with this law is the Minister. The Minister is accountable to the President and the People's Majlis on matters relating to that service.

[stamp] [signature]

(b) Issuing passports and electronic travel documents needed by Maldivian citizens to depart the Maldives and to return to the Maldives, and implementing matters related to that;

(c) Issuing permission for foreigners to come to and stay in the Maldives, cancelling that permission, and implementing all matters that must be carried out in relation to that permission;

(d) Sending back foreigners who come to the Maldives without permission, and deporting foreigners who live in the Maldives without permission to stay in the Maldives;

(e) Making and implementing the regulations and procedures required to be made under this law, in the manner set out in this law;

(f) Carrying out, within the scope set out in this law, all matters designated in this law as a responsibility of Maldives Immigration.

Controller General of Immigration
7. (a) The most senior person who plans all matters of carrying out the responsibilities and duties of Maldives Immigration and runs and oversees that service from day to day, and the person accountable for carrying out the responsibilities that Maldives Immigration must fulfil in implementing this law, is the Controller General of Immigration.

(b) In a manner not conflicting with the responsibilities designated in this law as the responsibility of the Controller General of Immigration, the Minister may give in writing to the Controller General the general guidance that needs to be given in order to implement the Maldives' immigration-related

