(c) In order to provide immigration services as set out in the law, establishing offices of Maldives Immigration in the regions of the Maldives, making arrangements for those offices to provide services, and seeking out and implementing ways to further strengthen and develop those services;

(d) Setting and implementing the principles and procedures that need to be set in carrying out the responsibilities of Maldives Immigration as set out in the law, issuing the orders that need to be issued in relation to those matters, and taking the measures that need to be taken;

(e) Carrying out the matters that Maldives Immigration must carry out in order to comply with the bilateral, regional and international treaties of the Maldives, and strengthening relations with and seeking cooperation from the relevant international organisations;

(f) Carrying out, within the scope of this law, all matters stated in this law as the responsibility of the Controller General of Immigration.

Removal of the Controller General from office and resignation
10. (a) The Controller General of Immigration may be removed from office if any of the following circumstances occurs.

(1) One of the attributes set out under subsection (b) of section 8 of this law as required to be fulfilled in the Controller General

[stamp] [signature]

being lacking;

(2) The Prosecutor General deciding to bring criminal charges against the Controller General, or the Controller General being accused, on the basis of reasonable evidence, of having committed a criminal offence, or of having participated in committing it, or of having assisted in it;

(3) Being unable to carry out the responsibilities of the post due to a health condition;

(4) Losing the trust needed to carry out the responsibilities of the Controller General because of committing an act contrary to the responsibilities of the post, or because of something done, or because of something left undone.

(b) If any of the circumstances set out in subsection (a) of this section occurs, the President has the power to remove the Controller General from office, based on a proposal submitted by the Minister to remove the Controller General from office, or even without a proposal from the Minister.

(c) If the Controller General wishes to resign from office, he must submit it in writing to the President, stating the reason.

(d) If the person holding the post of Controller General submits a resignation to the President under subsection (c) of this section, he shall leave office upon the President

