Performing duties with neutrality and adhering to standards of conduct and ethics
15. (a) Immigration officers must carry out the responsibilities and duties entrusted to them under this law free from conflicts of interest. And in decisions made by officers in relation to matters [unclear] to those officers, officers must not, whether politically or non-politically, work to advance their own personal interest or the interest of a party connected to those officers.

(b) Every officer of the Maldives must uphold the following basic standards of conduct in carrying out his responsibilities.

[stamp] [signature]

(1) Carrying out responsibilities and making the decisions that must be made without bowing to any party, without obtaining a benefit for any particular party, and remaining free from bias;

(2) Not discriminating on the basis of a person's race, nationality, colour, sex, physical or mental disability, political or other opinion, financial means, the family to which the person belongs or island of birth, the language the person speaks, or economic standing or status;

(3) Building the work on a foundation of equality, transparency and accountability;

(4) Not committing any act of corruption, not participating in such acts, reporting such acts, acting against such acts, and promoting and maintaining the integrity of the office in the workplace;

(5) Not disclosing in any other manner information obtained by a person in the capacity of the post, except in carrying out that person's duties and responsibilities and in the ways permitted by law;

(6) While in office and even after leaving office, in carrying out that person's post,

