Collection and Processing of Biometric Information
31. (a) Maldives Immigration has the power to collect and process the biometric information of every person arriving in and departing from the Maldives in granting immigration clearance under this Act.

(b) For the purpose of this section, "biometric information" shall have the meaning specified in subsection (d) of section 73 of this Act.

(c) The biometric information of persons arriving in the Maldives and persons departing from the Maldives collected under this Act may be used only for the following purposes.

(1) to verify the identity of that person;

(2) to store and maintain that information in order to carry out the responsibilities of immigration determined under this Act;

(3) for immigration to make a decision in relation to granting a permit to that person under this Act or in relation to that person in other matters as well.

(d) Every person arriving in and departing from the Maldives, other than Maldivian citizens, shall give immigration permission to collect that person's biometric information for use for the purposes specified in subsection (a) of this section.

(e) For the purpose of subsection (d) of this section, the methods by which biometric information may be collected, and the principles and procedures relating to the processing and storage of that information, shall be specified in the regulation made under this Act.

(f) In order to assess the extent to which the processing of biometric information collected under this Act may adversely affect the security and protection of data information, and the ways in which that can be reduced, immigration shall carry out a privacy impact assessment. And in carrying out such an assessment, it shall consult the Privacy Commissioner.

